    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d69-a4">

                <pb facs="0176" n="68" xml:id="pg68"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No.
                    66.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister of Foreign Affairs
                        to the Diplomatic Corps.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry for Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Bio
                                de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-10-24"><hi rendition="#italic">October 24,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have received the joint note which your excellency and the representatives of
                    Portugal, Italy, the United States of America, and France addressed to me
                    to-day, saying that they have been informed by the commanders of the naval
                    forces of their respective countries that the Federal Government is at the
                    present moment having cannon prepared in the marine arsenal and projectiles in
                    the war arsenal.</p>
                <p>I have brought to the knowledge of the Vice-President of the Republic the facts
                    set forth on this subject in the said note.</p>
                <p>Be pleased, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Carlos de
                    Carvalho</hi>,</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
